# Exhaustiveness: the summary block must be EXACTLY this. Any extra
# application section or changed resource fails here rather than being
# quietly pinned by the next --regenerate.
expect:affected=1 changed=1 resources=+0,-0,~2
# The CLASSIC HTTP(S) Chart.yaml dependency resolves, renders and diffs. Only an
# index-backed `helm dependency build` can produce these manifests - argocdf
# registers that repository in its throwaway helm home automatically - so this
# is the positive proof of that path. Its twin,
# case/oci-dependency-bump, covers the OCI dependency in the same chart, where
# the classic one is only proven negatively (an unresolved dependency would
# replace the whole diff with a render error).
must:helm\.sh/chart: classicdep-6\.7\.1
must:podinfo:6\.7\.1
# The OCI dependency beside it must NOT move: the two cases cross-guard, so a
# bump that leaked to both dependencies fails here and in oci-dependency-bump.
must-not:ocidep-6\.7\.1
# ---- log assertions (this case runs with --verbose; see its CASE_ARGS) ----------
# The umbrella chart declares dependencies and does not commit charts/, so ArgoCD's
# dependency PROBE fires here and only here: it runs `helm template`, lets it FAIL,
# then builds dependencies and templates again. util/exec logs that expected failure
# at ERROR before the caller decides it was harmless, so argocdf demotes it - and
# these three lines are the only end-to-end check of that, in either direction.
#
# It must reach the log DEMOTED, under the subprocess sub-prefix...
must-log:DEBU argocd/exec:.*missing in charts/ directory
# ...it must NOT be at ERROR, which is the half must-log alone cannot express: a
# demotion that stopped working would still satisfy the line above. This is also the
# tripwire for an argo-cd bump that changes the probe's message or the argv shape -
# the predicate would stop matching and the noise would return here.
must-not-log:ERRO argocd.*missing in charts/ directory
# ...and the --api-versions flood must be elided from that real argv (a live cluster
# contributes hundreds of pairs, ~16k characters, of which the failure is the last
# ~180). The count is kept, so this also proves argocdf passed the API set at all.
must-log:--api-versions <[0-9]+ elided>
